Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Text the Japanese ROM builds in code
Applies after 0060-japanese-game-logic.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

Where the Japanese ROM assembles a line from pieces its texts follow: the trade
question names both Pokémon, the player's then the partner's; the Pokédex
category takes the word for Pokémon with no space; the contest's appeal number goes in
front of its text; mail uses that ROM's layout and windows with the sender's name
before the word for "from"; the diploma prints the name, the Pokédex and the signature
apart. Battle Pyramid arrows (an escape code in that ROM's texts) and the Lilycove
Lady's texts need no code. Other languages are unchanged.

